  "findings": [
    "Original single-song export writes cached span files to an ACTION_CREATE_DOCUMENT output stream, without the full bulk tagging temporary file; it still retains original cache and does not establish full-span coverage or destination durability.",
    "Original bulk export prepares a full temporary tagged file and keeps the original cache; do not equate serialization with zero duplicate storage.",
    "SFTP-SAF Proxy.onWrite catches IOException but advances offset and returns the requested size; flush and close errors are also caught. A caller success is not proof of a complete remote file.",
    "Artmux at the selected source uses a pipe with an asynchronous SFTP writer. Its createDocument sends an empty file to the unguarded requested child path; the pinned JSch version defaults put(InputStream,String) to OVERWRITE, so an existing matching file can be overwritten.",
    "RSAF defaults to VFS write caching; its provider says a file may be buffered to disk, and upload can continue asynchronously after the client closes. Neither low phone-storage use nor completed remote upload is established by client close."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Static public source review; no provider, export, transfer, installation, credential, grant or device mutation was performed.",
    "Independent exact remote readback, source completeness, collision-safe creation and per-track identity/settlement remain required before any removal of an original.",
    "An unmodified installed NaTune app retains its original private downloads; a differently signed patched app has no demonstrated access to that private cache."
  ]
}
